            <ArticleTitle>Q&amp;A: Morphological insights into evolution.</ArticleTitle>
            <Pagination>
                <MedlinePgn>83</MedlinePgn>
            </Pagination>
            <ELocationID EIdType="doi" ValidYN="Y">10.1186/s12915-017-0425-z</ELocationID>
            <Abstract>
                <AbstractText>In this question and answer article we discuss how evolution shapes morphology (the shape and pattern of our bodies) but also how learning about morphology, and specifically how that morphology arises during development, can shed light on mechanisms that might allow change during evolution. For this we concentrate on recent findings from our lab on how the middle ear has formed in mammals.</AbstractText>
            </Abstract>
